1
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:25,605
Home alarms raise far more false alarms than real ones:

2
00:00:25,605 --> 00:00:28,961
police studies put them at 94 to 98 percent.

3
00:00:29,341 --> 00:00:32,205
And cloud cameras send private video out of the home.

4
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,048
SENTRIX is our answer.

5
00:00:35,428 --> 00:00:37,310
One small unit watches a room,

6
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:42,265
and decides on the device itself whether there is a handgun or a visible flame.

7
00:00:42,645 --> 00:00:46,748
It asks the owner before anyone else is alerted, and its video,

8
00:00:46,748 --> 00:00:49,223
faces and evidence stay on the device.

9
00:00:51,220 --> 00:01:00,230
Kartik led vision and the backend: turning detector scores into alarms we can trust, and the architecture of the whole system.

10
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:11,210
Akshay led identity: recognising residents per tracked person, body re-identification, and setting the match bars from error rates we measured.

11
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:20,020
Prashant led audio: capturing sound, tagging it with an AudioSet model, and aligning every sound window with the video.

12
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:29,230
Harshit led behaviour and fusion: the data-collection protocol, and the transparent rules that combine every input into one alarm level.

13
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:42,670
Mehul led records, interfaces and evaluation: tamper-evident evidence storage, the alarm screens, and judging the product by the alarm level a user actually sees.

14
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:49,694
This video follows the six parts of the guideline: the components, the connections,

15
00:01:49,694 --> 00:01:53,749
the inputs, how to start, stop and troubleshoot it, a complete run,

16
00:01:53,749 --> 00:01:55,081
and the final results.

17
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,137
SENTRIX has two programs.

18
00:01:58,517 --> 00:02:03,512
The device runs on a Raspberry Pi 5: it owns the camera, runs every model,

19
00:02:03,512 --> 00:02:05,334
and serves its own screens.

20
00:02:05,714 --> 00:02:10,826
The Portal runs in the cloud: it holds accounts, contacts and a responder desk,

21
00:02:10,826 --> 00:02:15,162
and reaches the device only through the device's own outbound link.

22
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:21,306
Inside the device, perception models produce votes: a YOLO person,

23
00:02:21,306 --> 00:02:26,868
weapon and fire detector, a DINOv2 scene classifier trained on our own footage,

24
00:02:26,868 --> 00:02:31,092
face recognition, body re-identification and a sound tagger.

25
00:02:31,472 --> 00:02:33,676
Evidence rules confirm the votes,

26
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:38,685
the threat confidence index and the level policy commit one of five levels,

27
00:02:38,685 --> 00:02:40,956
and the SOS engine asks the owner.

28
00:02:41,336 --> 00:02:45,554
Every message passes one send guard, and test mode is on by default.

29
00:02:47,050 --> 00:02:52,932
Our unit is a Raspberry Pi 5 with 8 GB of memory and an active cooler,

30
00:02:52,932 --> 00:02:56,714
powered by the official 27-watt USB-C supply.

31
00:02:57,094 --> 00:03:02,498
A Camera Module 3 sits on a tilting mount, a USB microphone listens,

32
00:03:02,498 --> 00:03:07,663
and three status LEDs show its state, all in our 3D-printed case.

33
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:13,158
The camera connects to the Pi's camera port with a ribbon cable,

34
00:03:13,158 --> 00:03:17,718
and the microphone goes into any USB port, even while SENTRIX is running.

35
00:03:18,098 --> 00:03:26,860
The green, amber and red LEDs are on GPIO 5, 12 and 13, through 330-ohm resistors.

36
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:31,370
The official 27-watt USB-C supply powers the Pi.

37
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:35,856
The README and the Pi guide in our repository list every pin.

38
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:42,279
SENTRIX needs a camera picture; sound from the USB microphone is optional.

39
00:03:42,659 --> 00:03:47,218
To set it up, the owner activates an account with a one-time code,

40
00:03:47,218 --> 00:03:51,709
and enters the home's address, the household, emergency contacts,

41
00:03:51,709 --> 00:03:55,232
who confirm by consent, and a PIN and a duress PIN.

42
00:03:55,612 --> 00:03:59,164
Residents' faces are enrolled from the device's own camera,

43
00:03:59,164 --> 00:04:02,656
so the people who live there are not treated as strangers.

44
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,975
On the Pi, SENTRIX is a service that starts by itself at boot,

45
00:04:07,975 --> 00:04:10,436
and the status command shows it running.

46
00:04:10,816 --> 00:04:15,525
The Portal is hosted on Render and always on, so there is nothing to start:

47
00:04:15,525 --> 00:04:17,974
the owner simply opens it in a browser.

48
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:22,028
The same service commands stop or restart it.

49
00:04:22,408 --> 00:04:26,121
The event log records every level change and every incident,

50
00:04:26,121 --> 00:04:29,339
and the doctor tool checks the models, the settings,

51
00:04:29,339 --> 00:04:33,424
the send guard and the evidence chain, without opening the camera.

52
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,722
Most problems have a short fix.

53
00:04:37,102 --> 00:04:39,261
No picture: reseat the camera ribbon.

54
00:04:39,641 --> 00:04:45,138
No sound: plug the microphone into any USB port; it is picked up automatically.

55
00:04:45,518 --> 00:04:49,828
Device shown offline: check the Wi-Fi; the link reconnects on its own.

56
00:04:50,208 --> 00:04:52,249
And if a room gives false alarms,

57
00:04:52,249 --> 00:04:56,888
the calibration tool sets that room's thresholds from the device's own log.

58
00:04:58,390 --> 00:05:02,277
Now a complete run, in test mode, so nothing can be sent anywhere.

59
00:05:02,657 --> 00:05:07,729
A held-out clip with a replica handgun, staged by our team, plays as the camera.

60
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:14,086
The scene model and the weapon detector both confirm the handgun, with a person in view.

61
00:05:14,466 --> 00:05:18,186
Level 3 is committed, and the device screen switches to the alert.

62
00:05:23,730 --> 00:05:28,611
On the owner's phone a red bar appears, and the alert puts the three answers first.

63
00:05:28,991 --> 00:05:31,335
The owner chooses Police and asks for help.

64
00:05:40,730 --> 00:05:43,770
The SENTRIX Desk, our simulated monitoring centre,

65
00:05:43,770 --> 00:05:48,025
receives the request with the address, the household and the snapshot,

66
00:05:48,025 --> 00:05:49,241
and acknowledges it.

67
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,730
The owner's phone now shows that the Desk is handling it.

68
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:58,284
The Desk closes the request with an outcome,

69
00:05:58,284 --> 00:06:01,349
and that outcome becomes a label for future training.

70
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:05,015
On the home network,

71
00:06:05,015 --> 00:06:09,351
the diagnostics page shows each model's score against its threshold,

72
00:06:09,351 --> 00:06:11,391
and how every input contributed.

73
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:19,645
And the owner can watch the live picture from anywhere, relayed through the Portal.

74
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:27,168
On the Raspberry Pi in our demo room, the same flow runs on four-second clips.

75
00:06:27,548 --> 00:06:31,1000
Its weapon and fire detectors are retrained on our own labelled recordings,

76
00:06:31,1000 --> 00:06:35,086
and its thresholds were set from the room's own log.

77
00:06:36,590 --> 00:06:37,401
Our results.

78
00:06:37,781 --> 00:06:44,651
Training on our own footage raised validation macro-F1 from 0.28 to 0.77,

79
00:06:44,651 --> 00:06:50,956
and cut false alarms from about fourteen to 0.79 per normal minute.

80
00:06:51,336 --> 00:06:53,948
The evidence rules then removed the rest,

81
00:06:53,948 --> 00:06:58,854
and re-deciding our first live session took Level 3 alarms from nine to none.

82
00:07:00,350 --> 00:07:03,747
Retrained on our own recordings,

83
00:07:03,747 --> 00:07:10,646
the detectors' held-out AUROC rose from 0.75 to 0.87 for weapons,

84
00:07:10,646 --> 00:07:16,697
and from 0.59 to 0.96 for fire, with no new false alarms.

85
00:07:17,077 --> 00:07:22,189
Eleven of fourteen weapon episodes and every flame reach Level 3 on replay.

86
00:07:22,569 --> 00:07:23,688
In the demo room,

87
00:07:23,688 --> 00:07:29,285
calibration took scene-model false alarms in a five-hour log from forty-nine to zero.

88
00:07:29,665 --> 00:07:33,962
And the Pi analyses a four-second clip in 3.9 seconds.

89
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:40,513
We also report the limits: too little normal footage to claim a false-alarm rate,

90
00:07:40,513 --> 00:07:43,819
a Pi that is still slower than its two-second target,

91
00:07:43,819 --> 00:07:47,375
and detectors that still need their own room calibration.

92
00:07:47,755 --> 00:07:50,426
Recording in the deployment room is our next step.

93
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:55,144
SENTRIX decides at home, and it asks the owner first.

94
00:07:55,524 --> 00:07:56,612
Thank you for watching.
